// expect: refuse E_OccursCheck
// The poly-recursion TEACH (§11 5.3, the question beats the guess):
// a shape the Mycroft rounds cannot stabilize — `bad` RETURNS x while
// self-calling at [x], so the recheck round meets ret ~ [ret] and the
// occurs refusal stands honestly (round 3's soundness working) — and
// the refusal carries T_PolyRecursionSignature naming the fn. The
// single-call fragment (see mn-poly-fragment) infers instead; this
// fixture pins the graceful K-exhausted floor.
fn bad(x, n) = if n <= 0 { x } else { bad([x], n - 1) }

fn main() = 0
